  <string name="onboarding_title">App blocking</string>
  <string name="onboarding_explain">Hush blocks apps itself, with an accessibility service. It only looks at which app is in front, and only acts while a session runs and the app is on one of your lists. Nothing leaves your phone.</string>
  <string name="onboarding_how_to">In Accessibility settings, open Downloaded apps (or Installed apps), choose Hush and turn it on. Then come back here. If the switch is greyed out, open App info for Hush, tap the three-dot menu and choose Allow restricted settings first.</string>
  <string name="onboarding_open_settings">Open Accessibility settings</string>
  <string name="onboarding_pick_apps">Blocking is on. Choose the apps each list blocks: Deep work during timer work phases, Detox during path levels.</string>
